30,2,1,talk,Minato,,It seems our developers are very busy and the coordination group is understaffed. We shouldn't pick something that adds more manual work for them.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,I found that network coverage at customer sites is very poor and getting device approval is slow. Any field-based app might face serious hurdles.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital budget is frozen, but we have some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses will get expensive as we scale.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"Interesting. It turns out tools requiring everyone to enter data daily usually fail, while specialized tools for one trade actually survive.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that staff are losing an hour a day just copying records, and we have delivery errors because different units have different addresses for the same supplier.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, that sounds like a lot of wasted time. Maybe we can find a way to help them without making more work for the coordinators?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@George, if the capital budget is frozen, we must avoid any proposal requiring heavy upfront hardware or infrastructure investment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"Precisely, Jonathan. We should favor something that fits within the recurring software allowance or uses fixed-fee production.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, your findings about copying records and misrouted deliveries suggest a need for a central hub, but we must ensure it isn't a ""daily entry"" trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree, May. We need a solution that solves the data duplication problem without becoming another chore that people eventually ignore.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried about the people. If we pick a big project, who will actually manage it if the coordination group is already empty?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We also have to consider that our in-house developers are unavailable until the third quarter. We cannot rely on them for a quick launch.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"If we avoid per-head licensing and stick to the software allowance, we can keep the costs predictable for next year's renewal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,"So we need something specialized, not a general tool for everyone, and something that doesn't require our internal developers immediately.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,It seems we are looking for a balance between solving these real floor-level inefficiencies and the technical and staffing constraints we've found.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
